* An ADF pipeline that normally completes in 20 minutes suddenly takes more than two hours. How would you investigate the issue and determine whether the source, destination, network, Integration Runtime, or pipeline configuration is responsible?
* Your ADF pipeline processes 10,000 files from Azure Blob Storage every night. One file fails while the remaining files succeed. How would you design the pipeline so that one failed file does not stop the entire batch?
* A production pipeline processes the same input file twice after an automatic retry, resulting in duplicate records in the target database. How would you identify the root cause and make the pipeline idempotent?
* Your business-critical ADF pipeline fails halfway through processing 500 tables. How would you design the recovery mechanism so that it resumes from the failed table instead of restarting everything?
* Your source database contains 500 million records, and the initial ADF migration is taking several days. How would you optimize the data movement and reduce the migration time?
* An incremental ADF pipeline is loading duplicate records every day. The pipeline uses a timestamp column as a watermark. How would you investigate the problem and redesign the incremental loading mechanism?
* A source application adds new columns to a table without notifying the data engineering team. The ADF pipeline starts failing because of schema mismatch. How would you handle schema evolution and prevent future failures?
* Your ADF pipeline successfully completes, but the target contains fewer records than the source. How would you investigate the data discrepancy and design reconciliation checks?
* A pipeline processes millions of records successfully but occasionally fails with timeout errors. How would you determine whether the problem is source performance, destination performance, network latency, or ADF configuration?
* Your organization wants to process files from an on-premises database and move them to Azure. How would you design the Integration Runtime and networking architecture?
* Your ADF pipeline uses a Self-hosted Integration Runtime, and production data movement suddenly stops. How would you troubleshoot the Integration Runtime and restore processing?
* A Java Spring Boot application needs to trigger an ADF pipeline whenever a business transaction is completed. How would you integrate the Java application with ADF and handle asynchronous pipeline execution?
* A Java service triggers an ADF pipeline but receives a successful response even though the actual pipeline later fails. How would you design the Java integration to correctly track pipeline execution status?
* Your company has hundreds of similar pipelines containing hard-coded database names, table names, and storage paths. How would you redesign the solution using metadata-driven and parameterized pipelines?
* Your ADF pipeline is consuming more Azure resources than expected, and the monthly data-integration cost has increased significantly. How would you identify the expensive activities and optimize the pipeline without affecting throughput?
* A pipeline processes thousands of files using ForEach. Increasing parallelism improves execution time but causes the source database to become overloaded. How would you determine the optimal parallelism?
* Your target database becomes unavailable while an ADF pipeline is processing data. When the database recovers, the pipeline must continue without creating duplicate records. How would you design retry, checkpointing, and idempotency?
* A business requires that every file arriving in Azure Blob Storage must be processed exactly once. How would you design the ADF architecture to track file processing state and prevent duplicate processing?
* Your ADF pipeline is successfully loading data, but downstream users complain that data is sometimes incomplete when they query it. How would you investigate pipeline timing, dependencies, transactions, and downstream availability?
* A production deployment changes an ADF pipeline and causes several dependent pipelines to fail. How would you design CI/CD, validation, rollback, and dependency management to prevent this type of incident?
* Your organization requires sensitive data to remain inside private Azure networking. How would you design ADF using Managed Identity, Private Endpoints, Key Vault, and appropriate network controls?
* A long-running ADF pipeline fails near completion after processing several hours of data. How would you design the pipeline to support restartability and checkpoint-based recovery?
* The source system produces files with inconsistent naming conventions and occasionally sends empty or corrupt files. How would you design an ADF pipeline to validate, quarantine, and process files safely?
* Your ADF pipeline processes data successfully, but downstream reconciliation shows mismatched totals between source and target. How would you identify whether records were lost, duplicated, filtered, or transformed incorrectly?
* Your organization needs near-real-time ingestion, but the current ADF solution runs every 15 minutes. How would you evaluate whether ADF is appropriate and redesign the architecture to meet the latency requirement?